Add PortfolioServer's commands to rpfolio: -x, -i, -q, -e, -m, -k, -s

PortfolioServer (SERVER.COM, github repository Atari-Portfolio_Server) replaces
the Portfolio's built-in file transfer server and adds commands it lacks.
This patch lets transfolio / rpfolio use them:

  -x PATTERN  Like -l, but lists folders too, with attributes, size, date
              and time, one entry per line:
                  d---- 0 2000-01-01 12:00:00 SUB
                  ----a 100 2000-01-01 12:00:00 SMALL.TXT
              (attributes: d folder, r read-only, h hidden, s system,
              a archive)
  -i          Show PortfolioServer's version and block size
  -q          Stop PortfolioServer
  -e PATH...  Erase (delete) files
  -m PATH...  Make folders
  -k PATH...  Remove empty folders
  -s DRIVE... Show free and total space, e.g. -s C: A:

-e, -m, -k and -s print one line per path and exit with code 1 if any
path failed (e.g. "Cannot delete C:\X.TXT: file not found (DOS error 2)").
Drive B: is refused, as it would make DOS ask for a disk on the Portfolio.

The built-in server acknowledges these commands but never replies; then
rpfolio says so and exits with code 3, so a caller can tell which server
is running. Everything else is unchanged.

The help text (rpfolio with no arguments, which doesn't touch the port)
includes the line "With PortfolioServer options, patch 1", so a caller such as
PiPortfolioDaemon can tell this build from the original one. The number
goes up when the options change.

Applies to https://github.com/skudi/transfolio at commit ab89073, on its
own or together with rpfolio-file-size.patch from PiPortfolioDaemon:

    git checkout ab89073
    git apply rpfolio-portfolioserver.patch
    cc -DRASPIWIRING -O3 transfolio.c -o rpfolio -lwiringPi

